From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add 15 AVPs from 3GPP TS 29.154
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

3GPP TS 29.154 V18.0.0 defines these AVPs in vendor 10415, which the
dictionary has no entry for at their codes:

  Network-Area-Info-List (4201): OctetString, clause 5.3.2
  Reference-Id (4202): OctetString, clause 5.3.3
  Transfer-Request-Type (4203): Unsigned32, clause 5.3.4
  Transfer-End-Time (4205): Time, clause 5.3.6
  Transfer-Start-Time (4206): Time, clause 5.3.7
  Transfer-Policy (4207): Grouped, 5 members, clause 5.3.8
  Transfer-Policy-Id (4208): Unsigned32, clause 5.3.9
  Number-Of-UEs (4209): Unsigned32, clause 5.3.10
  Access-Network-Reports (4210): Grouped, 10 members, clause A.6.3.2
  Event-Configuration (4211): Grouped, 4 members, clause A.6.3.3
  Event-Configuration-State (4212): Unsigned32, clause A.6.3.4
  Event-Configuration-Status (4213): Grouped, 2 members, clause A.6.3.5
  Event-Reporting-Results (4214): Unsigned32, clause A.6.3.6
  Event-Reports (4215): Grouped, 3 members, clause A.6.3.7
  Extended-SCEF-Reference-ID (4216): Unsigned64, clause A.6.3.8

Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

Not added here: Time-Window, code 4204, named like TS29.345's code 3818.
Wireshark names each display filter field after its AVP, so two entries
named alike need one renamed, as Cx-User-Data and Sh-User-Data are.

Generated by Seanchaí (integrations/wireshark/additions.py).
